---
layout: page
---
{%- comment -%}
  The CV page, rendered from _data/cv.json (generated from the LaTeX CV; never edited by hand).

  Markup contract (later CV tasks and the CV script build on it):
  - the wrapper: <div class="cv-page" data-landing="<page.landing_section>">. The CV script adds the class cv-js to it, and every
    "one section at a time" rule in _sass/_cv.scss is scoped under .cv-page.cv-js, so without the script every section shows.
  - the page header (.cv-top with the Updated line and the Download PDF link, then the .cv-stats line), then .cv-layout: the
    section panel beside .cv-sections.
  - the section panel: <nav class="cv-nav" aria-label="CV sections"> with one
    <a class="cv-nav-link" href="#<section id>" data-section="<section id>"> per section, holding the section title and, when the
    section has entries (counted across all its groups), <span class="cv-nav-count" aria-hidden="true">N</span> followed by a
    visually hidden ", N entries", so a screen reader reads "Publications, 11 entries". Without the script the links are in-page
    jumps; the script marks the current one with aria-current="true" and hides the other sections with the hidden attribute.
  - each section: <section class="cv-section" id="<section id>" aria-labelledby="<section id>-heading">,
    with <h2 class="cv-section-title" id="<section id>-heading">; sections listed in page.collapse_sections
    also carry data-collapse-after="<page.collapse_after>"
  - each group: <div class="cv-group" data-group="<group id>">, with an <h3 class="cv-group-title"> when it has a title
  - each entry: _includes/cv/entry.liquid (see there)
  - a section with publications also has, after its intro, <div class="cv-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter publications" hidden>
    holding <button type="button" class="cv-filter" data-filter="all|first-author|co-author|published|under-review" aria-pressed="true|false">;
    "all" starts pressed. The bar is hidden in the markup, so without JavaScript it is not shown; the CV script reveals it and filters
    the .cv-card elements by their data-status and data-first-author.

  Fields ending in _html are trusted, already-sanitised HTML and are output as is; every other string is escaped.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign cv = site.data.cv -%}
{%- assign stats = cv.stats -%}
{%- assign collapse_sections = page.collapse_sections -%}
<div
  class="cv-page"
  {% if page.landing_section %}
    data-landing="{{ page.landing_section | escape }}"
  {% endif %}
>
  <div class="cv-top">
    {% if cv.updated %}
      <p class="cv-updated">Updated {{ cv.updated | date: '%B %Y' }} · same version as the PDF</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if page.cv_pdf %}
      <a class="cv-download" href="{{ page.cv_pdf | relative_url }}" download><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span> Download PDF</a>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  {% if stats %}
    <p class="cv-stats">
      {% if stats.funding %}
        <span class="cv-stat"
          ><b class="cv-stat-value">{{ stats.funding | escape }}</b> <span class="cv-stat-label">funding awarded</span></span
        >
      {% endif %}
      {% if stats.citations %}
        <span class="cv-stat"
          ><b class="cv-stat-value">{{ stats.citations | escape }}</b>
          <span class="cv-stat-label"
            >citations{% if stats.hindex %} · h-index {{ stats.hindex | escape }}{% endif -%}
          </span></span
        >
      {% endif %}
      {% if stats.students %}
        <span class="cv-stat"
          ><b class="cv-stat-value">{{ stats.students | escape }}+</b> <span class="cv-stat-label">students taught</span></span
        >
      {% endif %}
    </p>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="cv-layout">
    <nav class="cv-nav" aria-label="CV sections">
      {% for section in cv.sections %}
        {%- assign entry_count = 0 -%}
        {%- for group in section.groups -%}
          {%- if group.entries -%}
            {%- assign entry_count = entry_count | plus: group.entries.size -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        <a class="cv-nav-link" href="#{{ section.id | escape }}" data-section="{{ section.id | escape }}">
          <span class="cv-nav-title">{{ section.title | escape }}</span>
          {%- if entry_count > 0 -%}
            <span class="cv-nav-count" aria-hidden="true">{{ entry_count }}</span>
            <span class="cv-sr-only"
              >, {{ entry_count }}
              {% if entry_count == 1 %}entry{% else %}entries{% endif -%}
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </nav>

    <div class="cv-sections">
      {% for section in cv.sections %}
        <section
          class="cv-section"
          id="{{ section.id | escape }}"
          aria-labelledby="{{ section.id | escape }}-heading"
          {% if collapse_sections contains section.id %}
            data-collapse-after="{{ page.collapse_after | escape }}"
          {% endif %}
        >
          <h2 class="cv-section-title" id="{{ section.id | escape }}-heading">{{ section.title | escape }}</h2>

          {% for paragraph in section.intro_html %}
            <p class="cv-intro">{{ paragraph }}</p>
          {% endfor %}

          {% assign has_pubs = false %}
          {% for group in section.groups %}
            {% for entry in group.entries %}
              {% if entry.pub %}
                {% assign has_pubs = true %}
              {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
          {% endfor %}
          {% if has_pubs %}
            <div class="cv-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter publications" hidden>
              <button type="button" class="cv-filter" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All</button>
              <button type="button" class="cv-filter" data-filter="first-author" aria-pressed="false">First author</button>
              <button type="button" class="cv-filter" data-filter="co-author" aria-pressed="false">Co-author</button>
              <button type="button" class="cv-filter" data-filter="published" aria-pressed="false">Published</button>
              <button type="button" class="cv-filter" data-filter="under-review" aria-pressed="false">Under review / preprint</button>
            </div>
          {% endif %}

          {% for group in section.groups %}
            {% if group.title or group.entries.size > 0 %}
              <div
                class="cv-group"
                {% if group.id %}
                  data-group="{{ group.id | escape }}"
                {% endif %}
              >
                {% if group.title %}
                  <h3 class="cv-group-title">{{ group.title | escape }}</h3>
                {% endif %}
                {% for entry in group.entries %}
                  {% include cv/entry.liquid entry=entry section=section %}
                {% endfor %}
              </div>
            {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}

          {% if section.footnotes_html.size > 0 %}
            <div class="cv-footnotes">
              {% for footnote in section.footnotes_html %}
                <p>{{ footnote }}</p>
              {% endfor %}
            </div>
          {% endif %}
        </section>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
